{"sections":[],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Articles and Tutorials","anchor":"Articles-and-Tutorials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Variants","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Exports","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Signals","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CustomTypes","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/BindingNodes","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RunningInEditor","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/MemoryManagement","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/TypesTranslation"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"General differences","type":"heading","anchor":"General-differences","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The SwiftGodot API follows the convention of the Swift platform, and one of the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"most notable places where this happens is in the use of camelCase style instead"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the snake_case style used in GDScript.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Enumerations and their values also change, for example, rather than having a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constant value like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CORNER_TOP_LEFT"},{"type":"text","text":" for the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Corner"},{"type":"text","text":" value, we use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Corner\/topLeft"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In Swift, function definitions take parameter names, and sometimes this","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"parameter name is omitted for the first argument. Instead of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"myNode.add_child(box)"},{"type":"text","text":", you would use "},{"code":"myNode.addChild (node: box)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Global-Scope","text":"Global Scope","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Global functions and some constants had to be moved to classes to avoid"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"polluting the global name space, and you can find them in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GD","isActive":true},{"text":" class.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Type-Mappings","level":2,"text":"Type Mappings","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Godot comes with some of their own data types like strings and dictionaries, but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"those types would clash with the existing Swift types with the same names.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is a list of the current data type mappings:"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GDScript type"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftGodot Name"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"String"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"GString","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Dictionary","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"VariantDictionary"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dictionary[Element]"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TypedDictionary"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Array","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"VariantArray"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Array[Element]","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"TypedArray","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/VariantArray","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a type-erased array that can hold any sort of element that can be managed by Godot."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In addition, there is a strongly-typed version of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"VariantArray","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" – ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/TypedArray","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" that holds specific type."}]},{"code":["let ints = TypedArray<Int>","let objects = TypedArray<Object?>"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Note that in the context of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Object","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"-derived classes only ","type":"text"},{"code":"Optional","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" elements are supported. That reflects exactly how Godot behaves. It allows ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s in "},{"code":"Object","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"-derived typed arrays, but not in other types.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Old Types","type":"heading","anchor":"Old-Types","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the past, we used different types for various functions which have now been unified, the old names of types that you might find in older documentation or samples are as follows:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"GArray","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", became "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"VariantArray"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"VariantCollection<BuiltinType>"},{"type":"text","text":", became "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TypedArray<BuiltinType>"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ObjectCollection<ObjectOrSubclassType>"},{"text":", became ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TypedArray<ObjectOrSubclassType?>"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"text":"GDScript Helper Functions","type":"heading","anchor":"GDScript-Helper-Functions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Many global helper functions that are exposed in GDScript have been exposed in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GD","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" class as static methods.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This means that you can invoke them like this:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["func reportError (error: Variant) {","    GD.printerr (msg)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Godot Math Functions","type":"heading","anchor":"Godot-Math-Functions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The various GDScript Math functions like "},{"code":"abs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"acos","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"atan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as well as their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"helper functions like ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clamp"},{"type":"text","text":" are defined as static functions in the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GD","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"class."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Generally, you can use the Swift versions instead of the GDScript versions,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"which are more complete and do not incurr a marshaling overhead.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Random-Functions","text":"Random Functions","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The random functions like "},{"code":"randi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"randf","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and under the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GD"},{"type":"text","text":" class. But Swift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"provides a set of random functions that are just as good, like"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/swift\/int\/random(in:)-9mjpw"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"or"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/swift\/double\/random(in:)-6idef","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that operate on Swift ranges."}]},{"text":"Idiom Mapping","anchor":"Idiom-Mapping","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"GDScript Idiom","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftGodot Equivalent","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"instance_from_id(n)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GD.instanceFromId (instanceId: n)"}]}]]]},{"anchor":"Checking-for-the-contents-of-a-variant","text":"Checking for the contents of a variant","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can check in one go if a given variant contains a valid object and is of a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"given type, with the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Variant\/asObject(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" method, combined with Swift’s"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"“let”:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["func demo(input: Variant) {","\tif let node = input.asObject(Node.self) {","\t\t\/\/ We have a happy node inside 'input'","\t} else {","\t\tprint (\"The variant did not wrap an object, if it did, it was either nil, or was not of type Node\")","\t}","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"@export annotations","level":2,"anchor":"export-annotations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@export"},{"type":"text","text":" annotation works the same way as it does in GDScript. Some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parameters and directives are different see the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Exports"},{"type":"text","text":" documentation"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"for additional information."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Signals","level":2,"text":"Signals"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Generally, use the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Signal"},{"type":"text","text":" macro to declare a new signal for your classes,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"like this:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["class Demo: Node {","    @Signal var livesChanged: SignalWithArguments<Int>","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For additional information on defining and connecting to signals see the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Signals","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" documentation.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"@onready annotation","anchor":"onready-annotation","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"GDScript supports an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@onready"},{"type":"text","text":" annotation on variables, like this:"}]},{"syntax":"gdscript","type":"codeListing","code":["@onready var my_label = get_node(\"MyLabel\")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This does not exist in SwiftGodot, to achieve a similar behavior, initialize"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"those variables in an overwritten "},{"code":"_ready","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method, so code like this:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@Godot","class Demo: Node {","\tvar myLabel: Node3D?","","\toverride func _ready () {","\t\tmyLabel = getNode (path: \"myLabel\") as? Node3D","\t}","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you do not need to load the node right away, and you merely need to be able","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"to access it, you can use this instead:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["class Demo: Node {","\t@BindNode var myLabel: Node3D","}"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Running code before nodes are added to the Scene Tree","anchor":"Running-code-before-nodes-are-added-to-the-Scene-Tree"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you need to run some code in your constructor, but overriding the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_ready()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function is already too late for you, you can use the following idiom:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Godot","class NetworkedNode: Node {","    required init() {","        super.init()","        onInit()","    }","","    required init(nativeHandle: UnsafeRawPointer) {","        super.init(nativeHandle: nativeHandle)","        onInit()","    }","","    func onInit() {","        print(\"Was init!\")","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Singletons","type":"heading","text":"Singletons","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Godot Singletons surface their API as static methods, to make the code more"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"shorter, for example:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let pressed = Input.isActionPressed(ui_down)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"However, in some very rare cases this is not enough. For example, you may want","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to access a member from the base class SwiftGodot.Object, like ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"connect"},{"type":"text","text":". For such"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"use cases we provide a static property named ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shared"},{"text":" that returns the singleton","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"instance.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let demo = Input.shared.joyConnectionChanged.connect { device, connected in ","   print (\"joyConnectionChanged called\")","}"]},{"type":"heading","text":"String","anchor":"String","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftGodot generally exposes a Swift-string based API, but there are some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"convenience methods that you might have come to expect from the Godot String"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"(things like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GString\/validateFilename"},{"type":"text","text":", those APIs are available in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/GString","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" class).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Callable","level":2,"anchor":"Callable","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In SwiftGodot, you can create "},{"code":"Callable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instances by directly passing a Swift function that takes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"borrowing Arguments"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"and returns a "},{"code":"Variant?","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" result, like this:"}]},{"code":["func myCallback(args: borrowing Arguments) -> Variant? {","\tprint (\"MyCallback invoked with \\(args.count) arguments\")","\tif let argument = try? arguments.argument(ofType: Int.self, at: 0) {","\t\tprint(\"First argument was an int: \\(argument)\")","\t}","\treturn nil","}","","let myCallable = Callable(myCallback)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For more convenience you can pass a closure containing arguments and return value that Godot can understand:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let myCallable = Callable { (int: Int, bool: Bool, object: Object?) -> Camera3D? in ","\t\/\/ do something ","\tif let camera = object as? Camera3D? {","\t\tif int > 2 || bool {","\t\t\treturn camera","\t\t}","\t}","","\treturn camera","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Conversion from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arguments"},{"type":"text","text":" to corresponding arguments will happen automatically. Or not, then function won’t be called and you will see a error log specifying what went wrong."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Alternatively, you can use a StringName that binds a method that you have exported (via, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Callable"},{"text":" macro), like this:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["@Callable func myCallback(message: String) {","\tGD.print(message)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can call the callable in GDScript by invoking call() method of the exported Swift type.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"GDScript","code":["MySwiftNode.myCallback.call(\"Hello from Swift!\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"AsyncAwait","type":"heading","text":"Async\/Await","level":2},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"⚠️ Note","anchor":"%E2%9A%A0%EF%B8%8F-Note","level":5},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The snippets below are using deprecated API and are dangerous. If signal never emits the Swift coroutine state will leak with all the captured context. Prefer using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Signal.connect"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GDScript comes with an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":" primitive, you can achieve similar functionality"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the Swift built-in await\/async stack.   Unlike GDScript, await can only be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"invoked from "},{"code":"async","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" methods.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This means that code like this wont work:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["func demo() {","\tawait someSignal.emitted","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For this to work, this needs to be in an async context, like this one:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["func demo() async {","\tawait someSignal.emitted","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you are inside of a function that is not async, you need to wrap your code in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Task, like this:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["func demo() {","\t\/\/ We are not an async function, but we can start a Task","\tTask {","\t\tawait someSignal.emitted","\t}","}"]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Differences","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot"]]},"schemaVe